# About Varda
  text: Varda’s W-Series vehicles are built, designed, and operated by Varda in-house, including the pharmaceutical processing payloads, the capsule
  text: From life-saving pharmaceuticals to more powerful fiber optics, there is a world of products used on Earth today that can only be manufactur
  text: Our team is uniquely suited to accomplishing this goal, with leadership and staff comprised of veterans from SpaceX, Blue Origin, major phar
  text: Varda is headquartered in El Segundo, California, where we have offices and a production facility where our vehicles, equipment, and materia
  text: Join Varda, and work to create a bustling in-space ecosystem.
# About this Role
  text: As a Supply Chain Planner, you will work closely with supply chain, manufacturing, production, and engineering to ensure on-time supply for 
  text: This full-time role is located in our El Segundo headquarters.
# Responsibilities
  text: Own demand and fulfilment planning for Varda capsule
  text: Ensure accurate lead times and inventory levels to enable production
  text: Maintain accurate configuration of assemblies through NPI changes
  text: Monitor inventory levels and the health of open orders, proactively addressing any issues or delays.
  text: Establish and monitor key metrics to track supply chain performance
  text: Conduct clear-to-build meetings with production and engineering teams
  text: Ensure demand is up to date with the latest engineering and lead times changes
  text: Define, manage, and continuously improve workflows within the ERP system
  text: Occasionally support placing purchase orders, fulfilling kits, and moving inventory as needed
# Basic Qualifications
  text: Material or production planning
  text: Operations or supply chain management
  text: Master production scheduling
  text: Some knowledge and understanding of ERP (enterprise resource planning) systems such as SAP, Oracle, Epicor etc
# Preferred Skills and Experience
  text: Aerospace experience is helpful
  text: Technical knowledge and skills in coding and computer applications, (e.g. MS Office Suite, VBA, Smartsheet, SQL, Confluence, JIRA, Power BI,
  text: Self-motivated, quick learner, and ability to prioritize efforts to meet customer and company goals
  text: Ability to develop and maintain strong internal and external supplier relationships in a fast-moving and ever-changing environment
  text: Exceptional analytical and organizational skills
  text: Excellent customer service skills, highly self-motivated
  text: Effective written, verbal and presentation communication skills
  text: Detail-oriented, and able to respond quickly to a fast-moving and ever-changing environment
# Pay Range
  text: This Position may be hired at an exempt or non-exempt level depending on candidate experience:
  text: Supply Chain Planner: 0-2 years of experience is a non-exempt hourly role. ($35.70-$48.30 per hour)
  text: Senior Supply Chain Planner: 2-4 years of experience is an exempt role ($92,820-$125,580 base salary).
  text: Leveling and base or hourly salary are determined by job-related skills, education level, experience level, and job performance
  text: You will be eligible for incentives in the form of stock options and/or long-term cash awards
# Benefits
  text: Consider your benefits covered for launch.
  text: Regular Full-Time Positions:
  text: Flexible PTO policy + 12 paid holidays
  text: 100% company-paid Medical, Dental, and Vision insurance plans for employees and dependents with FSA and employer-matched HSA options
  text: Voluntary accident, hospital, critical illness, and pet insurance
  text: $120/month wellness reimbursement for gym and fitness expenses
  text: 12 weeks of parental leave (with supplemental disability leave for CA mothers)
  text: Family building, pregnancy, parenting and menopause benefits via Maven Clinic
  text: Sponsored One Medical memberships for employees and their dependents
  text: Substantial incentive equity in a fully funded space start-up
  text: 401(k) retirement plan with 6% employer match (immediately vested)
  text: $20/pay period cell phone reimbursement
  text: Relocation support for new hires, if needed
  text: Workplace Experience & Perks
  text: Fully stocked kitchen with lunch provided daily and dinner provided twice weekly
  text: Company and team-bonding events, happy hours and mission-success celebrations
  text: Up to $4,000 gross up in relocation support, if eligible
  text: Up to $850 commute credit through Lyft or car rental reimbursement, if eligible
